{"name":"Nacre","hex":"#e8e2d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nacre","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shellfish which contains mother-of-pearl. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A pearly substance made mainly of stacked layers of aragonite and organic matter which lines the interior of many shells; mother-of-pearl."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nacre"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nacre","blocks":[{"text":"Nacre, also known as mother-of-pearl, is an organic–inorganic composite material produced by some molluscs as an inner shell layer. It is also the material of which pearls are composed. It is strong, resilient, and iridescent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/NautilusCutawayLogarithmicSpiral.jpg/330px-NautilusCutawayLogarithmicSpiral.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nacre","wikidata":"Q215865"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Masa_per%C5%82owa3.jpg/330px-Masa_per%C5%82owa3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Masa_per%C5%82owa3.jpg/330px-Masa_per%C5%82owa3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nacreous shell worked into a decorative object","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMasa_per%C5%82owa3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Nacre_microscopic_structure.png/500px-Nacre_microscopic_structure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Nacre_microscopic_structure.png/500px-Nacre_microscopic_structure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Schematic of the microscopic structure of nacre layers","link":"https